# Build context for BOTH recipes in this directory (Dockerfile and, when the
# context happens to be this tree, Dockerfile.crew).
#
# container_tests/ is the image's own test suite: ~4,000 lines exercising a Linux
# container's supervisor. Nothing COPYs it and nothing in the image could run it,
# so it is pure context upload on every build. MANIFEST.in excludes it from the
# sdist for the same reason and says so at length; this is the same rule applied
# to the other place the tree gets packaged up and shipped somewhere.
container_tests/

# Never in an image, never in a context.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]

# NOT excluded, deliberately, so the notes below survive a future edit:
#   vendor/    holds the single staged wheel, read through the Dockerfile's
#              `--mount=type=bind,source=vendor`. A bind mount reads from the
#              build context, so excluding it here breaks the build with a
#              missing-mount error rather than a missing-file one.
#   container/ is COPYed wholesale and is the running code.
